# Two Avatar's Wraths, one from each player. Bot1's, turn 1, targets its own Giver of Runes, which is spared ("all other
# creatures": there are none). Bot2, barred only from zones other than its hand, casts Snapcaster Mage and its own Wrath
# from its hand in turn 2 with no target: that airbends Giver of Runes and Snapcaster Mage (CR 701.65a) and bars Bot1 until
# Bot2's next turn (CR 611.2b, 611.2c), while Bot1's Wrath bars Bot2 only until Bot1's turn 3 begins.
# Turn 3: Bot2's restriction has ended, so in Bot1's upkeep it casts the flash Snapcaster from exile for {2}; Bot1's has not,
# so in its own main phase, with {2} open, its Giver of Runes is refused. Turn 5, Bot2's restriction on Bot1 over, Bot1 casts
# Giver from exile for {2}: the control.

